      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's about twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Doses that high raise the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum). This may be what you meant, since 1700 mg is double 850 mg.\n- **1700 mg per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg per dose**, or another dose.\n- **1700 mg three times daily as written**, if there's a reason I'm missing. Please confirm, and I'll enter it with a note recording that you verified the dose.\n\nOnce you tell me the dose, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
